{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794529051563,"sessionID":"ses_e2dbc3ae5ffes1Ef3Xp19Y6IEG","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2444376002yb0pg6ve1HyljQ","sessionID":"ses_e2dbc3ae5ffes1Ef3Xp19Y6IEG","messageID":"msg_1d244378a0010Vj0dtfR2HCHr1","type":"tool","id":"call_ae29936a8d694be9b8c1fb77","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md, lines 1-284\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 5: recommendation-contract-and-brief\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that generate one command table, fill four recommendation fields, print the command and its policy in the brief, state the degraded contract, fix the reach check and retire the legacy ids.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"recommendation contract and brief tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 5: recommendation-contract-and-brief\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: \n26: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n27: \n28: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise.\n29: - `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `HK` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks`.\n30: - `D` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`. `G` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json`.\n31: - `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`. `R` is `$ADV/lib/render.ts`. `H` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`. `SCH` is `$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`. `CLI` is `$ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts`. `PY` is `$ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py`. `FB` is `$HK/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`.\n32: - `RC` is `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.cjs`. `RT` is `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.test.cjs`.\n33: - `REC` is `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --format json --json`.\n34: - `C` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. `M` is `jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .attachedMetrics.plain, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.typed_same_owner_ambiguous'`.\n35: - `P` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`.\n36: - `ROLL` is `jq -c '[.commandPolicies | group_by(.command)[] | (map(.policy) | if index(\"ask\") then \"ask\" elif index(\"start\") then \"start\" else \"run\" end)] | group_by(.) | map({(.[0]): length}) | add' $G`.\n37: - `S` is this phase's `scratch/` folder. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0 with no output.\n38: \n39: Each task is one change to the files it names. No task reads holdout prompt text. A relabel edits a label field by row id and prints no prompt.\n40: \n41: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. A task that runs `node $D` rewrites the generated blocks in `CA`, `R`, `$ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, `PY` and `G`, so no other task in its wave touches those files.\n42: - Wave 0: T001, T002, T003, T004, T005, T054, T055. Read-only setup, each writes its own `$S` file.\n43: - Gate: no task from wave 1 on starts before the coordinator confirms that phase 007's before-measurement on the branch tip is done.\n44: - Wave 1: T006 (`CA`), T007 (`SCH`), T008 (`subprocess.ts`), T009 (`PY`), T010 (`projection.ts`), T011 (`RC`).\n45: - Wave 2: T012 (`D`, regenerates), T013 (`FB`), T014 (schema test), T015 (`RT`).\n46: - Wave 3: T016 (`H`), T017 (`R`), T018 (`CLI`).\n47: - Wave 4: T019 (`H`), T020 (`D`, `R`, regenerates).\n48: - Wave 5: T021, T022, T023, T024, T025, T026. One test file group each.\n49: - Wave 6: T027 (`D`, `allow-list.json`), T028 (`scoring-compatibility.json`), T029 (`explicit.ts`), T030 (`fusion.ts`), T031 (`scoring-constants.ts`), T032 (`PY`), T033 (same-owner test).\n50: - Wave 7: T034 (`D` run, regenerates), T035 (relabel script and the four label files).\n51: - Wave 8: T036 (`PY`), T037 (rebuild and the command baseline file), T038, T039, T040 (one doc each).\n52: - Wave N1: T056 (the one source file T055 names, and `D` run when that file is a deriver input).\n53: - Wave N2: T057 (rebuild and the command baseline file).\n54: - CARRY-003 wave C1: T041 (`$S` probe), T042 (activation fixture test), T043 (`system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json`).\n55: - CARRY-003 wave C2: T044 (`ambiguity.ts`), T045 (`D` run, regenerates).\n56: - CARRY-003 wave C3: T046.\n57: - Verification, one at a time: T047 to T053.\n58: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n59: \n60: ---\n61: \n62: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n63: ## Phase 1: Setup\n64: \n65: - [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$S/before.txt`). Verify: `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]`, `node $C | $M` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, the plain block with tune combined 9 and holdout combined 0, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` and `[\"cmd-create-agent-typed-01\"]`, and `$ROLL` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n66: - [x] T002 Write `$S/brief-heads.mjs`, which pipes six prompts through `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` and prints the first line of each `additionalContext`, and save its output (`$S/brief-heads-before.txt`). The prompts are the five non-skipped hook prompts in the `spec.md` measured block plus `research caching strategies in depth over several iterations`. Verify: the file has six lines, and the first reads `Advisor: live; use command-spec-kit-plan 0.82/0.16 pass.`\n67: - [x] T003 Copy `../003-plain-chat-command-reach/scratch/hook-latency.mjs` to `$S/hook-latency.mjs` and run it three times (`$S/hook-latency-before-{1,2,3}.json`). Verify: `jq -c '[.n,.medianMs,.p95Ms]'` on each file prints 44 and two numbers.\n68: - [x] T004 Run the reach check with Ollama up (`$S/reach-before.txt`). Verify: `curl -s localhost:11434/api/tags | jq -r '.models[].name'` lists `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, and `node $RC --hub sk-doc` exits 1 with `outranked=4` and `RESULT: FAILED`.\n69: - [x] T005 Run the suite once (`$S/suite-before.txt`). Verify: `npm test` in `ADV` prints a summary line, and the file records its failed count.\n70: - [x] T054 Write `$S/nm-sk-doc-probe.mjs`, which sets `VITEST`, imports `scoreAdvisorPrompt` from `$ADV/dist/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.js` and prints, for `sk-doc`, `system-skilled-doctor`, `sk-code` and `sk-design`, the confidence, the score and each positive lane contribution with its evidence, for the prompt of row `nm-sk-doc-01`. Save the output (`$S/nm-sk-doc-before.txt`). Verify: the output matches the probe block in `spec.md`, with `sk-doc` absent and `sk-code` holding `token:typo` and `token:heading`.\n71: - [x] T055 Trace each token in `$S/nm-sk-doc-before.txt` to the source file and field it is projected from, by reading how `$ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/lexical.ts` and `$ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` build a skill's token list, and record why `sk-doc` holds no documentation-edit token (`$S/nm-sk-doc-source.txt`). Verify: the file has one line per token `typo`, `heading`, `guide`, `setup` and `debug`, each naming skill, file and field, and one line naming the `sk-doc` source field that should carry documentation-edit vocabulary.\n72: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n77: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n78: \n79: ### Wave 1\n80: - [x] T006 [P] In `CA`, add `export interface CommandRow { readonly command: string; readonly policy?: 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'; readonly ownerSkillId: string }`, an empty marked block `// BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` holding `export const COMMAND_ROWS: Readonly<Record<string, CommandRow>> = {};` and `export const COMMAND_POLICIES: Readonly<Record<string, 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'>> = {};` then `// END GENERATED COMMAND ROWS`, and `export function commandRowFor(id: string): CommandRow | undefined` that reads `COMMAND_ROWS` with `Object.hasOwn`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -c \"GENERATED COMMAND ROWS\" $CA` prints 2.\n81: - [x] T007 [P] In `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` (`SCH`), add `kind: z.enum(['skill', 'command']).optional()`, `policy: z.enum(['run', 'start', 'ask']).optional()` and `ownerSkillId: z.string().min(1).optional()`. Leave `command` and `.strict()` as they are. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"^  (kind|policy|ownerSkillId):\" $SCH` prints the three new lines.\n82: - [x] T008 [P] In `AdvisorRecommendation` (`$ADV/lib/subprocess.ts`), add `readonly command?: string`, `readonly policy?: string` and `readonly ownerSkillId?: string`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0.\n83: - [x] T009 [P] Delete the `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` and `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGE_OWNER_NORMALIZATION` dictionaries from `PY`. Verify: `rg -n \"HAND_AUTHORED\" $ADV --glob '!dist'` prints nothing, `python3 -m py_compile $PY` exits 0 and `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py` exits 0.\n84: - [x] T010 [P] In `$ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, change `readonly routingEnabled?: boolean;` to `readonly routingEnabled: boolean;` and the filter in `scoringCommandBridges` to `bridge.routingEnabled === true`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"readonly routingEnabled: boolean;\" $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints one line.\n85: - [x] T011 [P] In `rankShippedFleet` (`RC`), set `hit` true when `shipped[0].skillId === hub` or `shipped[0].ownerSkillId === hub`, and set `present` true when any shipped entry has `skillId === hub` or `ownerSkillId === hub`. Change nothing else. Verify: `node $RT` exits 0 and prints `[sk-doc] router reach shipped-fleet ranking passed`.\n86: \n87: ### Wave 2\n88: - [x] T012 In `D`, add `renderCommandRows(entries, policies)` and register `CA`'s `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block in `generatedSources`. Emit one `COMMAND_ROWS` row per id a scorer can return for an enabled entry: its TypeScript id, its Python id and its entry id. `command` is the doctor runnable string from `DOCTOR_DETAILS` or the entry's `command`. `policy` is the `commandPolicies` record whose route matches the runnable's target, or the route-null record. When the runnable names no target and the command has several route records, take the strictest of `ask`, `start` and `run`. `ownerSkillId` is the entry's `skillId`. Emit `COMMAND_POLICIES` keyed by runnable string the same way. Run `node $D`. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, `rg -n \"'command-doctor-update': \\{ command: '/doctor:update', policy: 'ask'\" $CA` prints one line, `rg -n \"'command-speckit-search': \\{ command: '/speckit:search', policy: 'run'\" $CA` prints one line, `rg -n \"'create:agent': \\{ command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'\" $CA` prints one line and `$TC` exits 0.\n89: - [x] T013 [P] In `recommendationFromCli` (`FB`), keep `value.kind` when it is `skill` or `command` (default `skill`), keep `value.policy` when it is `run`, `start` or `ask`, and keep `value.ownerSkillId` when it is a non-empty string. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-no-match.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n90: - [x] T014 [P] In `$ADV/tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts`, add one case that parses a recommendation with all four fields and one that rejects it with `consequence: 'x'` added. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n91: - [x] T015 [P] In `RT`, add two cases through the stand-in advisor: a `create:agent` row with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'` first and `sk-doc` second counts as a hit for `--hub sk-doc`, and a `command-doctor-git-hooks` row with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-git'` first and `sk-doc` second still prints `outranked`. Verify: `node $RT` exits 0.\n92: \n93: ### Wave 3\n94: - [x] T016 In `publicRecommendation` (`H`), add `kind: recommendation.kind`, and when `commandRowFor(recommendation.skill)` returns a row, add its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0, and after `npm run build` in `ADV`, `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"save context\"}' | jq '[.data.recommendations[] | select(.command == \"/speckit:save\")] | length'` prints 1.\n95: - [x] T017 In `R`, render the label of a recommendation that has a command, from its fields or else from `commandRowFor(skill)`, as `<ownerSkillId or skill> → <command> (<policy>)`, dropping the parenthesis when no policy is known. Use it for the `use` head and both sides of the `ambiguous` head. Every part passes `sanitizeSkillLabel`. Rewrite `doctorCommandString` to return `commandRowFor(id)?.command` for a doctor id. Leave the `Also:` line's trigger unchanged. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS\\[\" $R` prints nothing.\n96: - [x] T018 In `CLI`, pass the prompt to `degradedRecommendations` and export it. For an entry with a `commandRowFor(entry.skill)` row: when the prompt contains the row's bare slash command (the text before the first space), emit `skillId`, `kind: 'command'`, `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId`. Otherwise emit the row's `ownerSkillId` as `skillId` with `kind: 'skill'`, and drop it when that skill is already in the list. Verify: `$TC` exits 0.\n97: \n98: ### Wave 4\n99: - [x] T019 In `enrichCompiledRoutes` (`H`), build `alreadyOffered` from the `command` fields of the recommendations and delete `BRIDGE_COMMAND_BY_ID`. When a hub gets an attached command, also set `policy: COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` when that key exists. Verify: after `npm run build` in `ADV`, `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\",\"options\":{\"includeCompiledRoute\":true}}' | jq -c '.data.recommendations[0] | {skillId,command,policy}'` prints `{\"skillId\":\"sk-doc\",\"command\":\"/create:readme\",\"policy\":\"start\"}`, and `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n100: - [x] T020 Delete `renderDoctorCommandStrings` and the `R` entry from `generatedSources` in `D`, then delete the `GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS` block from `R`, then run `node $D`. Verify: `rg -n \"GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS|renderDoctorCommandStrings\" $D $R` prints nothing, `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh` and `$TC` exits 0.\n101: \n102: ### Wave 5\n103: - [x] T021 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts`. It renders six constructed results through `renderAdvisorBrief` and asserts the six heads in `plan.md` section 3 exactly, that each head before `\\nDirectives:` is at most 320 characters and that no head contains `command-`. Add one row each for a missing field filled from `COMMAND_ROWS`, an id with no row and a missing policy. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n104: - [x] T022 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/cli-degraded-command-contract.vitest.ts`. It calls the exported `degradedRecommendations` with a typed prompt `/speckit:save this session` over a `command-speckit-save` entry and expects `command` `/speckit:save` and `policy` `start`, then with `create a readme for the utils folder` over `sk-doc` and `command-create-readme` entries and expects one `sk-doc` entry with no `command`. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/cli-degraded-command-contract.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n105: - [x] T023 [P] In `$ADV/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts`, add a case where the CLI JSON row is `{\"skillId\":\"command-speckit-save\",\"confidence\":0.89,\"uncertainty\":0.12}` with no new field, and assert the rendered head contains `system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start)`. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n106: - [x] T024 [P] In `$ADV/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts` and `$ADV/tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts`, change each expected doctor head to the new label form, such as `sk-git → /doctor:git hooks (ask)`, and nothing else. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n107: - [x] T025 [P] In `$ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-renderer.vitest.ts` and `$ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-brief-producer.vitest.ts`, change each expected head that named a command row to the new label form, and nothing else. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy` reports 0 failed.\n108: - [x] T026 [P] In the files under `$ADV/tests/hooks/` other than the envelope test, change each expected head that named a command row to the new label form, and nothing else. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks` reports 0 failed.\n109: \n110: ### Wave 6\n111: - [x] T027 [P] Remove the allow-list read, its drop rule for matching metadata entries and the `allowList` count from `D`, and delete `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json`. Do not run `D`. Verify: `rg -n \"allow-list|allowList\" $D` prints nothing and `test ! -e $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json` exits 0.\n112: - [x] T028 [P] In `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json`, delete the four `python` rows whose `id` is `command-spec-kit-plan`, `-complete`, `-implement` or `-resume`, and the `command-spec-kit-resume` key of `pythonOwnerNormalization`. Verify: `jq -c '[.python[].id | select(test(\"^command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)$\"))]' $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` prints `[]`.\n113: - [x] T029 [P] In `$ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts`, replace `command-spec-kit-resume` with `command-speckit-resume` on its two lines. Verify: `rg -c \"command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)\" $ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts` prints nothing.\n114: - [x] T030 [P] In `$ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, replace each `command-spec-kit-plan` or `command-spec-kit-resume` with `command-speckit-plan` or `command-speckit-resume`. Verify: `rg -c \"command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)\" $ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts` prints nothing.\n115: - [x] T031 [P] In `$ADV/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts`, replace `command-spec-kit-plan` with `command-speckit-plan` in its comment. Verify: `rg -c \"command-spec-kit-plan\" $ADV/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts` prints nothing.\n116: - [x] T032 [P] In `PY`, outside the generated blocks, replace each of the four `command-spec-kit-*` ids with its `command-speckit-*` id. Leave `SPECKIT_COMMAND_BRIDGE_PREFIXES` and the deep ids alone. Verify: `rg -n \"command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)\" $PY` prints only lines inside `BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND BRIDGES`, which T034 regenerates.\n117: - [x] T033 [P] In `$ADV/tests/scorer/same-owner-ambiguity.vitest.ts`, replace the two old ids with their new ids. Verify: `rg -c \"command-spec-kit-\" $ADV/tests/scorer/same-owner-ambiguity.vitest.ts` prints nothing.\n118: \n119: ### Wave 7\n120: - [x] T034 Run `node $D`. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -c '{status, counts}'` prints `fresh` with no `allowList` key and `typescriptActive` 45, `jq -c '[.entries[] | .runtime.typescript.id, .runtime.python.id] | map(select(. != null and test(\"^command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)$\")))' $G` prints `[]`, and `$ROLL` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n121: - [x] T035 [P] Write `$S/relabel-ids.mjs`, which rewrites any JSON string value equal to one of the four old ids to its new id in `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/holdout-prompts.jsonl`, `$ADV/scripts/fixtures/gate2-golden-prompts.jsonl`, `$ADV/scripts/fixtures/skill-advisor-regression-cases.jsonl` and `$ADV/tests/parity/fixtures/local-native-approved-divergences.json`, never prints a prompt and writes file, row id and field per change to `$S/relabel-list.txt`. Run it. Verify: `rg -c \"command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)\\b\"` over the four files prints nothing, and `wc -l < $S/relabel-list.txt` prints 5.\n122: \n123: ### Wave 8\n124: - [ ] T036 [P] In `PY`, delete the `\"/prompt\": [(\"sk-prompt\", 3.2)]` lexical row and the `if command == \"/prompt\":` branch of `_command_bridge_owner`. Verify: `rg -n '\"/prompt\"' $PY` prints nothing and `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py` exits 0.\n125: - [ ] T037 [P] Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, then `node $C --write`. Verify: `node $C | $M` prints the T001 lines, and `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]`.\n126: - [ ] T038 [P] Describe the head form and the degraded contract in `$HK/skill-advisor-hook.md`. Verify: `rg -n \"→ /speckit:save \\(start\\)|degraded\" $HK/skill-advisor-hook.md` prints at least two lines.\n127: - [ ] T039 [P] Describe `kind`, `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`. Verify: `rg -c \"ownerSkillId\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md` prints at least 1.\n128: - [ ] T040 [P] In `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md`, describe the `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block and remove the allow-list as a live source. Verify: `rg -n \"COMMAND_ROWS\" $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` prints a line and `rg -n \"allow-list.json\" $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` prints nothing.\n129: \n130: ### Wave N1\n131: - [ ] T056 Make one correction at the source T055 names: remove a token a skill holds only through a harvest artifact, or add a general documentation-edit term to the `sk-doc` source field T055 names. The change adds no string of two or more consecutive words from the `nm-sk-doc-01` prompt. When the file is a deriver input, run `node $D`. Verify: for each two-word window of the prompt, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- <changed file> | rg -F \"<window>\"` prints nothing, `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, and after `npm run build` in `ADV`, `node $S/nm-sk-doc-probe.mjs` prints `sk-doc` with the highest score.\n132: \n133: ### Wave N2\n134: - [ ] T057 Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, then `node $C --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.rows[\"nm-sk-doc-01\"] | {top, offered}' $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` prints `{\"top\":\"sk-doc\",\"offered\":false}`, `node $C | $M` prints typed at least 24 of 44, tune combined at least 9 of 45, holdout combined at least 0 of 44 and false offers 0 of 35, and `$P` prints numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` with false fire no higher than 5. If any is worse, revert T056 and mark it `[B]` with the printed numbers.\n135: \n136: ### CARRY-003 wave C1\n137: - [ ] T041 [P] CARRY-003 (a): write `$S/agent-ambiguity.mjs`, which sets `VITEST`, imports `scoreAdvisorPrompt` from `$ADV/dist/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.js` and prints `ambiguous` and, for the top four rows, `skill`, `confidence`, `score`, `confidenceFloored` and the length of `ambiguousWith`, for `/create:agent dependency-auditor for release checks`. Save the output (`$S/agent-ambiguity.txt`). Verify: the output shows the top row `create:agent` with `confidenceFloored` true clustered with floored rows. If it shows a different cause, mark T044 `[B]` with that cause.\n138: - [ ] T042 [P] CARRY-003 (b): in `$ADV/tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts`, add a case that builds a fixture skills root through the file's existing fixture seam with one standalone skill whose `command-metadata.json` declares a command that `scoring-compatibility.json` does not list, and asserts the derived entry is enabled for both `typescript` and `python`. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n139: - [ ] T043 [P] CARRY-003 (c): add `which packets mention` to `userIntent.ownedSignals` of `/speckit:search` in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json`. Verify: `jq -c '.[] | select(.command == \"/speckit:search\") | .userIntent.ownedSignals | index(\"which packets mention\")' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json` prints a number.\n140: \n141: ### CARRY-003 wave C2\n142: - [ ] T044 CARRY-003 (a): in `clustersWithTop` (`$ADV/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts`), when both the top and the member carry `confidenceFloored`, cluster on the score margin alone. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/scorer` reports 0 failed and `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]`. If `$P` moves, revert the change and mark this task `[B]` with the printed numbers.\n143: - [ ] T045 Run `node $D`. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`.\n144: \n145: ### CARRY-003 wave C3\n146: - [ ] T046 Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, then `node $C --write`. Verify: `node $C | $M` prints `[]` as its fourth line with the first three lines as in T001, `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]`, and `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"show me which packets mention the token cap\"}' | jq -c '[.data.recommendations[] | select(.command == \"/speckit:search\") | .policy]'` prints `[\"run\"]`.\n147: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n148: \n149: ---\n150: \n151: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n152: ## Phase 3: Verification\n153: \n154: - [ ] T047 Run `npm run build` in `ADV` and in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime`. Verify: `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"save context\"}' | jq '[.data.recommendations[] | select(.command == \"/speckit:save\")] | length'` prints 1, and `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"/speckit:plan add a login page\"}' | jq -c '.data.recommendations[0] | {kind,command,policy,ownerSkillId}'` prints `{\"kind\":\"command\",\"command\":\"/speckit:plan\",\"policy\":\"start\",\"ownerSkillId\":\"system-spec-kit\"}`.\n155: - [ ] T048 Run `node $S/brief-heads.mjs > $S/brief-heads-after.txt`. Verify: the first line reads `Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:plan (start) 0.82/0.16 pass.`, the git hooks line contains `/doctor:git hooks (ask)`, and `rg -c \"command-\" $S/brief-heads-after.txt` prints nothing.\n156: - [ ] T049 With Ollama up, run `node $RC --hub sk-doc > $S/reach-after.txt`. Verify: it exits 0 and prints `outranked=0` and `RESULT: PASSED`.\n157: - [ ] T050 Run `$S/hook-latency.mjs` three times (`$S/hook-latency-after-{1,2,3}.json`). Verify: the middle median is at most 25 ms over the T003 middle median and the middle p95 at most 40 ms over the T003 middle p95.\n158: - [ ] T051 Run every gate. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, `$ROLL` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`, `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]`, `$TC` exits 0, `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py` exits 0, `node $RT` exits 0, `node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs | tail -1` reports `failed=0` and `npm test` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\n159: - [ ] T052 Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md` exits 0, and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#).*(specs/|REQ-0|T0[0-9]{2}|CARRY-003)\"` prints nothing.\n160: - [ ] T053 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n161: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n162: \n163: ---\n164: \n165: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n166: ## Completion Criteria\n167: \n168: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`, or the CARRY-003 tasks T041 to T046 removed by an operator decision to drop the group\n169: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n170: - [ ] The six golden briefs pass and `save context` returns one entry carrying `/speckit:save`. The reach check prints `RESULT: PASSED`\n171: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n172: \n173: ---\n174: \n175: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n176: ## Cross-References\n177: \n178: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n179: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n180: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n181: - **Review**: `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md`\n182: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n183: \n184: ---\n185: \n186: ## Verification Checklist\n187: \n188: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n189: ## Verification Protocol\n190: \n191: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n192: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n193: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n194: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n195: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n196: \n197: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A moved pinned number blocks the phase.\n198: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n199: \n200: ---\n201: \n202: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n203: ## Pre-Implementation\n204: \n205: - [x] CHK-001 [P0] The before numbers, brief heads, reach check, timing and suite are in `$S` (T001 to T005). Evidence: `before.txt`, `brief-heads-before.txt`, `reach-before.txt`, `hook-latency-before-{1,2,3}.json` (middle median 179.86 ms, middle p95 240.23 ms) and `suite-before.txt` (1482 passed, 0 failed).\n206: - [x] CHK-002 [P0] The four design questions have an operator answer. Evidence: 2026-11-12, each the recommended option, recorded in `spec.md` section 10.\n207: - [x] CHK-003 [P1] The operator keeps CARRY-003. Evidence: \"Carry three, settle five (Recommended)\".\n208: - [x] CHK-004 [P0] The coordinator confirmed phase 007's before-measurement is done before wave 1 started. Evidence: 144 of 144 runs in `../007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl`, last runtime finished 2026-11-12T23:30:58Z, wave 1 dispatched after it.\n209: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n210: \n211: ---\n212: \n213: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n214: ## Code Quality\n215: \n216: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `$TC` exits 0.\n217: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number or a task id (T052).\n218: - [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Every command string and policy a reader shows comes from the generated table, and none is hand-kept.\n219: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] A missing field, an unknown id or a missing policy renders without an error (T021).\n220: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n221: \n222: ---\n223: \n224: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n225: ## Testing Checklist\n226: \n227: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] The schema test and the six golden briefs pass (T014, T021).\n228: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The floors hold (T037, T051).\n229: - [ ] CHK-022 [P1] The degraded and older-daemon cases pass (T022, T023).\n230: - [ ] CHK-023 [P1] The reach check passes with real embeddings, and the other-hub fixture still fails (T015, T049).\n231: - [ ] CHK-024 [P1] `nm-sk-doc-01` tops at `sk-doc` with no recall or pinned number lower (T057).\n232: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n233: \n234: ---\n235: \n236: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n237: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n238: \n239: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] The gap is class `contract`: the public output lacks fields its readers need.\n240: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every reader of the old doctor block is updated: `rg -n \"DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS|doctorCommandString\" $ADV --glob '!dist'`.\n241: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Every reader of `ownerSkillId` and `command` is listed: `rg -n \"ownerSkillId|\\.command\\b\" $ADV $HK .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts --glob '!dist' --glob '!node_modules'`.\n242: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The renderer matrix axes from `plan.md` are each a test row.\n243: - [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on.\n244: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n245: \n246: ---\n247: \n248: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n249: ## Security\n250: \n251: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] Every label part passes `sanitizeSkillLabel`.\n252: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] The relabel script prints no prompt text (T035).\n253: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n254: \n255: ---\n256: \n257: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n258: ## Documentation\n259: \n260: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same fields and numbers.\n261: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The hook doc, the feature catalog entry and the bridges README match the code (T038 to T040).\n262: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n263: \n264: ---\n265: \n266: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n267: ## File Organization\n268: \n269: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Probes, timing runs, the relabel script and capture output live in `scratch/` only.\n270: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n271: \n272: ---\n273: \n274: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n275: ## Verification Summary\n276: \n277: | Category | Total | Verified |\n278: |----------|-------|----------|\n279: | P0 Items | 12 | 1/12 |\n280: | P1 Items | 11 | 1/11 |\n281: | P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n282: \n283: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-12\n284: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md, lines 1-284\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 5: recommendation-contract-and-brief\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that generate one command table, fill four recommendation fields, print the command and its policy in the brief, state the degraded contract, fix the reach check and retire the legacy ids.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"recommendation contract and brief tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 5: recommendation-contract-and-brief\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: \n26: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n27: \n28: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise.\n29: - `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `HK` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks`.\n30: - `D` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`. `G` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json`.\n31: - `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`. `R` is `$ADV/lib/render.ts`. `H` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`. `SCH` is `$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`. `CLI` is `$ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts`. `PY` is `$ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py`. `FB` is `$HK/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`.\n32: - `RC` is `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.cjs`. `RT` is `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.test.cjs`.\n33: - `REC` is `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --format json --json`.\n34: - `C` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. `M` is `jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .attachedMetrics.plain, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.typed_same_owner_ambiguous'`.\n35: - `P` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`.\n36: - `ROLL` is `jq -c '[.commandPolicies | group_by(.command)[] | (map(.policy) | if index(\"ask\") then \"ask\" elif index(\"start\") then \"start\" else \"run\" end)] | group_by(.) | map({(.[0]): length}) | add' $G`.\n37: - `S` is this phase's `scratch/` folder. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0 with no output.\n38: \n39: Each task is one change to the files it names. No task reads holdout prompt text. A relabel edits a label field by row id and prints no prompt.\n40: \n41: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. A task that runs `node $D` rewrites the generated blocks in `CA`, `R`, `$ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, `PY` and `G`, so no other task in its wave touches those files.\n42: - Wave 0: T001, T002, T003, T004, T005, T054, T055. Read-only setup, each writes its own `$S` file.\n43: - Gate: no task from wave 1 on starts before the coordinator confirms that phase 007's before-measurement on the branch tip is done.\n44: - Wave 1: T006 (`CA`), T007 (`SCH`), T008 (`subprocess.ts`), T009 (`PY`), T010 (`projection.ts`), T011 (`RC`).\n45: - Wave 2: T012 (`D`, regenerates), T013 (`FB`), T014 (schema test), T015 (`RT`).\n46: - Wave 3: T016 (`H`), T017 (`R`), T018 (`CLI`).\n47: - Wave 4: T019 (`H`), T020 (`D`, `R`, regenerates).\n48: - Wave 5: T021, T022, T023, T024, T025, T026. One test file group each.\n49: - Wave 6: T027 (`D`, `allow-list.json`), T028 (`scoring-compatibility.json`), T029 (`explicit.ts`), T030 (`fusion.ts`), T031 (`scoring-constants.ts`), T032 (`PY`), T033 (same-owner test).\n50: - Wave 7: T034 (`D` run, regenerates), T035 (relabel script and the four label files).\n51: - Wave 8: T036 (`PY`), T037 (rebuild and the command baseline file), T038, T039, T040 (one doc each).\n52: - Wave N1: T056 (the one source file T055 names, and `D` run when that file is a deriver input).\n53: - Wave N2: T057 (rebuild and the command baseline file).\n54: - CARRY-003 wave C1: T041 (`$S` probe), T042 (activation fixture test), T043 (`system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json`).\n55: - CARRY-003 wave C2: T044 (`ambiguity.ts`), T045 (`D` run, regenerates).\n56: - CARRY-003 wave C3: T046.\n57: - Verification, one at a time: T047 to T053.\n58: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n59: \n60: ---\n61: \n62: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n63: ## Phase 1: Setup\n64: \n65: - [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$S/before.txt`). Verify: `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]`, `node $C | $M` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, the plain block with tune combined 9 and holdout combined 0, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` and `[\"cmd-create-agent-typed-01\"]`, and `$ROLL` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n66: - [x] T002 Write `$S/brief-heads.mjs`, which pipes six prompts through `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` and prints the first line of each `additionalContext`, and save its output (`$S/brief-heads-before.txt`). The prompts are the five non-skipped hook prompts in the `spec.md` measured block plus `research caching strategies in depth over several iterations`. Verify: the file has six lines, and the first reads `Advisor: live; use command-spec-kit-plan 0.82/0.16 pass.`\n67: - [x] T003 Copy `../003-plain-chat-command-reach/scratch/hook-latency.mjs` to `$S/hook-latency.mjs` and run it three times (`$S/hook-latency-before-{1,2,3}.json`). Verify: `jq -c '[.n,.medianMs,.p95Ms]'` on each file prints 44 and two numbers.\n68: - [x] T004 Run the reach check with Ollama up (`$S/reach-before.txt`). Verify: `curl -s localhost:11434/api/tags | jq -r '.models[].name'` lists `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, and `node $RC --hub sk-doc` exits 1 with `outranked=4` and `RESULT: FAILED`.\n69: - [x] T005 Run the suite once (`$S/suite-before.txt`). Verify: `npm test` in `ADV` prints a summary line, and the file records its failed count.\n70: - [x] T054 Write `$S/nm-sk-doc-probe.mjs`, which sets `VITEST`, imports `scoreAdvisorPrompt` from `$ADV/dist/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.js` and prints, for `sk-doc`, `system-skilled-doctor`, `sk-code` and `sk-design`, the confidence, the score and each positive lane contribution with its evidence, for the prompt of row `nm-sk-doc-01`. Save the output (`$S/nm-sk-doc-before.txt`). Verify: the output matches the probe block in `spec.md`, with `sk-doc` absent and `sk-code` holding `token:typo` and `token:heading`.\n71: - [x] T055 Trace each token in `$S/nm-sk-doc-before.txt` to the source file and field it is projected from, by reading how `$ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/lexical.ts` and `$ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` build a skill's token list, and record why `sk-doc` holds no documentation-edit token (`$S/nm-sk-doc-source.txt`). Verify: the file has one line per token `typo`, `heading`, `guide`, `setup` and `debug`, each naming skill, file and field, and one line naming the `sk-doc` source field that should carry documentation-edit vocabulary.\n72: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n77: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n78: \n79: ### Wave 1\n80: - [x] T006 [P] In `CA`, add `export interface CommandRow { readonly command: string; readonly policy?: 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'; readonly ownerSkillId: string }`, an empty marked block `// BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` holding `export const COMMAND_ROWS: Readonly<Record<string, CommandRow>> = {};` and `export const COMMAND_POLICIES: Readonly<Record<string, 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'>> = {};` then `// END GENERATED COMMAND ROWS`, and `export function commandRowFor(id: string): CommandRow | undefined` that reads `COMMAND_ROWS` with `Object.hasOwn`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -c \"GENERATED COMMAND ROWS\" $CA` prints 2.\n81: - [x] T007 [P] In `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` (`SCH`), add `kind: z.enum(['skill', 'command']).optional()`, `policy: z.enum(['run', 'start', 'ask']).optional()` and `ownerSkillId: z.string().min(1).optional()`. Leave `command` and `.strict()` as they are. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"^  (kind|policy|ownerSkillId):\" $SCH` prints the three new lines.\n82: - [x] T008 [P] In `AdvisorRecommendation` (`$ADV/lib/subprocess.ts`), add `readonly command?: string`, `readonly policy?: string` and `readonly ownerSkillId?: string`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0.\n83: - [x] T009 [P] Delete the `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` and `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGE_OWNER_NORMALIZATION` dictionaries from `PY`. Verify: `rg -n \"HAND_AUTHORED\" $ADV --glob '!dist'` prints nothing, `python3 -m py_compile $PY` exits 0 and `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py` exits 0.\n84: - [x] T010 [P] In `$ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, change `readonly routingEnabled?: boolean;` to `readonly routingEnabled: boolean;` and the filter in `scoringCommandBridges` to `bridge.routingEnabled === true`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"readonly routingEnabled: boolean;\" $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints one line.\n85: - [x] T011 [P] In `rankShippedFleet` (`RC`), set `hit` true when `shipped[0].skillId === hub` or `shipped[0].ownerSkillId === hub`, and set `present` true when any shipped entry has `skillId === hub` or `ownerSkillId === hub`. Change nothing else. Verify: `node $RT` exits 0 and prints `[sk-doc] router reach shipped-fleet ranking passed`.\n86: \n87: ### Wave 2\n88: - [x] T012 In `D`, add `renderCommandRows(entries, policies)` and register `CA`'s `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block in `generatedSources`. Emit one `COMMAND_ROWS` row per id a scorer can return for an enabled entry: its TypeScript id, its Python id and its entry id. `command` is the doctor runnable string from `DOCTOR_DETAILS` or the entry's `command`. `policy` is the `commandPolicies` record whose route matches the runnable's target, or the route-null record. When the runnable names no target and the command has several route records, take the strictest of `ask`, `start` and `run`. `ownerSkillId` is the entry's `skillId`. Emit `COMMAND_POLICIES` keyed by runnable string the same way. Run `node $D`. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, `rg -n \"'command-doctor-update': \\{ command: '/doctor:update', policy: 'ask'\" $CA` prints one line, `rg -n \"'command-speckit-search': \\{ command: '/speckit:search', policy: 'run'\" $CA` prints one line, `rg -n \"'create:agent': \\{ command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'\" $CA` prints one line and `$TC` exits 0.\n89: - [x] T013 [P] In `recommendationFromCli` (`FB`), keep `value.kind` when it is `skill` or `command` (default `skill`), keep `value.policy` when it is `run`, `start` or `ask`, and keep `value.ownerSkillId` when it is a non-empty string. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-no-match.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n90: - [x] T014 [P] In `$ADV/tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts`, add one case that parses a recommendation with all four fields and one that rejects it with `consequence: 'x'` added. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n91: - [x] T015 [P] In `RT`, add two cases through the stand-in advisor: a `create:agent` row with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'` first and `sk-doc` second counts as a hit for `--hub sk-doc`, and a `command-doctor-git-hooks` row with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-git'` first and `sk-doc` second still prints `outranked`. Verify: `node $RT` exits 0.\n92: \n93: ### Wave 3\n94: - [x] T016 In `publicRecommendation` (`H`), add `kind: recommendation.kind`, and when `commandRowFor(recommendation.skill)` returns a row, add its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0, and after `npm run build` in `ADV`, `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"save context\"}' | jq '[.data.recommendations[] | select(.command == \"/speckit:save\")] | length'` prints 1.\n95: - [x] T017 In `R`, render the label of a recommendation that has a command, from its fields or else from `commandRowFor(skill)`, as `<ownerSkillId or skill> → <command> (<policy>)`, dropping the parenthesis when no policy is known. Use it for the `use` head and both sides of the `ambiguous` head. Every part passes `sanitizeSkillLabel`. Rewrite `doctorCommandString` to return `commandRowFor(id)?.command` for a doctor id. Leave the `Also:` line's trigger unchanged. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS\\[\" $R` prints nothing.\n96: - [x] T018 In `CLI`, pass the prompt to `degradedRecommendations` and export it. For an entry with a `commandRowFor(entry.skill)` row: when the prompt contains the row's bare slash command (the text before the first space), emit `skillId`, `kind: 'command'`, `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId`. Otherwise emit the row's `ownerSkillId` as `skillId` with `kind: 'skill'`, and drop it when that skill is already in the list. Verify: `$TC` exits 0.\n97: \n98: ### Wave 4\n99: - [x] T019 In `enrichCompiledRoutes` (`H`), build `alreadyOffered` from the `command` fields of the recommendations and delete `BRIDGE_COMMAND_BY_ID`. When a hub gets an attached command, also set `policy: COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` when that key exists. Verify: after `npm run build` in `ADV`, `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\",\"options\":{\"includeCompiledRoute\":true}}' | jq -c '.data.recommendations[0] | {skillId,command,policy}'` prints `{\"skillId\":\"sk-doc\",\"command\":\"/create:readme\",\"policy\":\"start\"}`, and `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n100: - [x] T020 Delete `renderDoctorCommandStrings` and the `R` entry from `generatedSources` in `D`, then delete the `GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS` block from `R`, then run `node $D`. Verify: `rg -n \"GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS|renderDoctorCommandStrings\" $D $R` prints nothing, `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh` and `$TC` exits 0.\n101: \n102: ### Wave 5\n103: - [x] T021 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts`. It renders six constructed results through `renderAdvisorBrief` and asserts the six heads in `plan.md` section 3 exactly, that each head before `\\nDirectives:` is at most 320 characters and that no head contains `command-`. Add one row each for a missing field filled from `COMMAND_ROWS`, an id with no row and a missing policy. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n104: - [x] T022 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/cli-degraded-command-contract.vitest.ts`. It calls the exported `degradedRecommendations` with a typed prompt `/speckit:save this session` over a `command-speckit-save` entry and expects `command` `/speckit:save` and `policy` `start`, then with `create a readme for the utils folder` over `sk-doc` and `command-create-readme` entries and expects one `sk-doc` entry with no `command`. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/cli-degraded-command-contract.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n105: - [x] T023 [P] In `$ADV/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts`, add a case where the CLI JSON row is `{\"skillId\":\"command-speckit-save\",\"confidence\":0.89,\"uncertainty\":0.12}` with no new field, and assert the rendered head contains `system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start)`. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n106: - [x] T024 [P] In `$ADV/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts` and `$ADV/tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts`, change each expected doctor head to the new label form, such as `sk-git → /doctor:git hooks (ask)`, and nothing else. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n107: - [x] T025 [P] In `$ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-renderer.vitest.ts` and `$ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-brief-producer.vitest.ts`, change each expected head that named a command row to the new label form, and nothing else. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy` reports 0 failed.\n108: - [x] T026 [P] In the files under `$ADV/tests/hooks/` other than the envelope test, change each expected head that named a command row to the new label form, and nothing else. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks` reports 0 failed.\n109: \n110: ### Wave 6\n111: - [x] T027 [P] Remove the allow-list read, its drop rule for matching metadata entries and the `allowList` count from `D`, and delete `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json`. Do not run `D`. Verify: `rg -n \"allow-list|allowList\" $D` prints nothing and `test ! -e $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json` exits 0.\n112: - [x] T028 [P] In `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json`, delete the four `python` rows whose `id` is `command-spec-kit-plan`, `-complete`, `-implement` or `-resume`, and the `command-spec-kit-resume` key of `pythonOwnerNormalization`. Verify: `jq -c '[.python[].id | select(test(\"^command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)$\"))]' $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` prints `[]`.\n113: - [x] T029 [P] In `$ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts`, replace `command-spec-kit-resume` with `command-speckit-resume` on its two lines. Verify: `rg -c \"command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)\" $ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts` prints nothing.\n114: - [x] T030 [P] In `$ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, replace each `command-spec-kit-plan` or `command-spec-kit-resume` with `command-speckit-plan` or `command-speckit-resume`. Verify: `rg -c \"command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)\" $ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts` prints nothing.\n115: - [x] T031 [P] In `$ADV/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts`, replace `command-spec-kit-plan` with `command-speckit-plan` in its comment. Verify: `rg -c \"command-spec-kit-plan\" $ADV/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts` prints nothing.\n116: - [x] T032 [P] In `PY`, outside the generated blocks, replace each of the four `command-spec-kit-*` ids with its `command-speckit-*` id. Leave `SPECKIT_COMMAND_BRIDGE_PREFIXES` and the deep ids alone. Verify: `rg -n \"command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)\" $PY` prints only lines inside `BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND BRIDGES`, which T034 regenerates.\n117: - [x] T033 [P] In `$ADV/tests/scorer/same-owner-ambiguity.vitest.ts`, replace the two old ids with their new ids. Verify: `rg -c \"command-spec-kit-\" $ADV/tests/scorer/same-owner-ambiguity.vitest.ts` prints nothing.\n118: \n119: ### Wave 7\n120: - [x] T034 Run `node $D`. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -c '{status, counts}'` prints `fresh` with no `allowList` key and `typescriptActive` 45, `jq -c '[.entries[] | .runtime.typescript.id, .runtime.python.id] | map(select(. != null and test(\"^command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)$\")))' $G` prints `[]`, and `$ROLL` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n121: - [x] T035 [P] Write `$S/relabel-ids.mjs`, which rewrites any JSON string value equal to one of the four old ids to its new id in `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/holdout-prompts.jsonl`, `$ADV/scripts/fixtures/gate2-golden-prompts.jsonl`, `$ADV/scripts/fixtures/skill-advisor-regression-cases.jsonl` and `$ADV/tests/parity/fixtures/local-native-approved-divergences.json`, never prints a prompt and writes file, row id and field per change to `$S/relabel-list.txt`. Run it. Verify: `rg -c \"command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)\\b\"` over the four files prints nothing, and `wc -l < $S/relabel-list.txt` prints 5.\n122: \n123: ### Wave 8\n124: - [ ] T036 [P] In `PY`, delete the `\"/prompt\": [(\"sk-prompt\", 3.2)]` lexical row and the `if command == \"/prompt\":` branch of `_command_bridge_owner`. Verify: `rg -n '\"/prompt\"' $PY` prints nothing and `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py` exits 0.\n125: - [ ] T037 [P] Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, then `node $C --write`. Verify: `node $C | $M` prints the T001 lines, and `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]`.\n126: - [ ] T038 [P] Describe the head form and the degraded contract in `$HK/skill-advisor-hook.md`. Verify: `rg -n \"→ /speckit:save \\(start\\)|degraded\" $HK/skill-advisor-hook.md` prints at least two lines.\n127: - [ ] T039 [P] Describe `kind`, `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`. Verify: `rg -c \"ownerSkillId\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md` prints at least 1.\n128: - [ ] T040 [P] In `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md`, describe the `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block and remove the allow-list as a live source. Verify: `rg -n \"COMMAND_ROWS\" $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` prints a line and `rg -n \"allow-list.json\" $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` prints nothing.\n129: \n130: ### Wave N1\n131: - [ ] T056 Make one correction at the source T055 names: remove a token a skill holds only through a harvest artifact, or add a general documentation-edit term to the `sk-doc` source field T055 names. The change adds no string of two or more consecutive words from the `nm-sk-doc-01` prompt. When the file is a deriver input, run `node $D`. Verify: for each two-word window of the prompt, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- <changed file> | rg -F \"<window>\"` prints nothing, `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, and after `npm run build` in `ADV`, `node $S/nm-sk-doc-probe.mjs` prints `sk-doc` with the highest score.\n132: \n133: ### Wave N2\n134: - [ ] T057 Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, then `node $C --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.rows[\"nm-sk-doc-01\"] | {top, offered}' $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` prints `{\"top\":\"sk-doc\",\"offered\":false}`, `node $C | $M` prints typed at least 24 of 44, tune combined at least 9 of 45, holdout combined at least 0 of 44 and false offers 0 of 35, and `$P` prints numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` with false fire no higher than 5. If any is worse, revert T056 and mark it `[B]` with the printed numbers.\n135: \n136: ### CARRY-003 wave C1\n137: - [ ] T041 [P] CARRY-003 (a): write `$S/agent-ambiguity.mjs`, which sets `VITEST`, imports `scoreAdvisorPrompt` from `$ADV/dist/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.js` and prints `ambiguous` and, for the top four rows, `skill`, `confidence`, `score`, `confidenceFloored` and the length of `ambiguousWith`, for `/create:agent dependency-auditor for release checks`. Save the output (`$S/agent-ambiguity.txt`). Verify: the output shows the top row `create:agent` with `confidenceFloored` true clustered with floored rows. If it shows a different cause, mark T044 `[B]` with that cause.\n138: - [ ] T042 [P] CARRY-003 (b): in `$ADV/tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts`, add a case that builds a fixture skills root through the file's existing fixture seam with one standalone skill whose `command-metadata.json` declares a command that `scoring-compatibility.json` does not list, and asserts the derived entry is enabled for both `typescript` and `python`. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n139: - [ ] T043 [P] CARRY-003 (c): add `which packets mention` to `userIntent.ownedSignals` of `/speckit:search` in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json`. Verify: `jq -c '.[] | select(.command == \"/speckit:search\") | .userIntent.ownedSignals | index(\"which packets mention\")' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json` prints a number.\n140: \n141: ### CARRY-003 wave C2\n142: - [ ] T044 CARRY-003 (a): in `clustersWithTop` (`$ADV/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts`), when both the top and the member carry `confidenceFloored`, cluster on the score margin alone. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/scorer` reports 0 failed and `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]`. If `$P` moves, revert the change and mark this task `[B]` with the printed numbers.\n143: - [ ] T045 Run `node $D`. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`.\n144: \n145: ### CARRY-003 wave C3\n146: - [ ] T046 Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, then `node $C --write`. Verify: `node $C | $M` prints `[]` as its fourth line with the first three lines as in T001, `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]`, and `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"show me which packets mention the token cap\"}' | jq -c '[.data.recommendations[] | select(.command == \"/speckit:search\") | .policy]'` prints `[\"run\"]`.\n147: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n148: \n149: ---\n150: \n151: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n152: ## Phase 3: Verification\n153: \n154: - [ ] T047 Run `npm run build` in `ADV` and in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime`. Verify: `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"save context\"}' | jq '[.data.recommendations[] | select(.command == \"/speckit:save\")] | length'` prints 1, and `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"/speckit:plan add a login page\"}' | jq -c '.data.recommendations[0] | {kind,command,policy,ownerSkillId}'` prints `{\"kind\":\"command\",\"command\":\"/speckit:plan\",\"policy\":\"start\",\"ownerSkillId\":\"system-spec-kit\"}`.\n155: - [ ] T048 Run `node $S/brief-heads.mjs > $S/brief-heads-after.txt`. Verify: the first line reads `Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:plan (start) 0.82/0.16 pass.`, the git hooks line contains `/doctor:git hooks (ask)`, and `rg -c \"command-\" $S/brief-heads-after.txt` prints nothing.\n156: - [ ] T049 With Ollama up, run `node $RC --hub sk-doc > $S/reach-after.txt`. Verify: it exits 0 and prints `outranked=0` and `RESULT: PASSED`.\n157: - [ ] T050 Run `$S/hook-latency.mjs` three times (`$S/hook-latency-after-{1,2,3}.json`). Verify: the middle median is at most 25 ms over the T003 middle median and the middle p95 at most 40 ms over the T003 middle p95.\n158: - [ ] T051 Run every gate. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, `$ROLL` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`, `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]`, `$TC` exits 0, `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py` exits 0, `node $RT` exits 0, `node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs | tail -1` reports `failed=0` and `npm test` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\n159: - [ ] T052 Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md` exits 0, and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#).*(specs/|REQ-0|T0[0-9]{2}|CARRY-003)\"` prints nothing.\n160: - [ ] T053 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n161: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n162: \n163: ---\n164: \n165: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n166: ## Completion Criteria\n167: \n168: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`, or the CARRY-003 tasks T041 to T046 removed by an operator decision to drop the group\n169: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n170: - [ ] The six golden briefs pass and `save context` returns one entry carrying `/speckit:save`. The reach check prints `RESULT: PASSED`\n171: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n172: \n173: ---\n174: \n175: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n176: ## Cross-References\n177: \n178: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n179: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n180: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n181: - **Review**: `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md`\n182: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n183: \n184: ---\n185: \n186: ## Verification Checklist\n187: \n188: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n189: ## Verification Protocol\n190: \n191: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n192: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n193: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n194: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n195: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n196: \n197: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A moved pinned number blocks the phase.\n198: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n199: \n200: ---\n201: \n202: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n203: ## Pre-Implementation\n204: \n205: - [x] CHK-001 [P0] The before numbers, brief heads, reach check, timing and suite are in `$S` (T001 to T005). Evidence: `before.txt`, `brief-heads-before.txt`, `reach-before.txt`, `hook-latency-before-{1,2,3}.json` (middle median 179.86 ms, middle p95 240.23 ms) and `suite-before.txt` (1482 passed, 0 failed).\n206: - [x] CHK-002 [P0] The four design questions have an operator answer. Evidence: 2026-11-12, each the recommended option, recorded in `spec.md` section 10.\n207: - [x] CHK-003 [P1] The operator keeps CARRY-003. Evidence: \"Carry three, settle five (Recommended)\".\n208: - [x] CHK-004 [P0] The coordinator confirmed phase 007's before-measurement is done before wave 1 started. Evidence: 144 of 144 runs in `../007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl`, last runtime finished 2026-11-12T23:30:58Z, wave 1 dispatched after it.\n209: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n210: \n211: ---\n212: \n213: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n214: ## Code Quality\n215: \n216: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `$TC` exits 0.\n217: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number or a task id (T052).\n218: - [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Every command string and policy a reader shows comes from the generated table, and none is hand-kept.\n219: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] A missing field, an unknown id or a missing policy renders without an error (T021).\n220: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n221: \n222: ---\n223: \n224: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n225: ## Testing Checklist\n226: \n227: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] The schema test and the six golden briefs pass (T014, T021).\n228: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The floors hold (T037, T051).\n229: - [ ] CHK-022 [P1] The degraded and older-daemon cases pass (T022, T023).\n230: - [ ] CHK-023 [P1] The reach check passes with real embeddings, and the other-hub fixture still fails (T015, T049).\n231: - [ ] CHK-024 [P1] `nm-sk-doc-01` tops at `sk-doc` with no recall or pinned number lower (T057).\n232: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n233: \n234: ---\n235: \n236: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n237: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n238: \n239: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] The gap is class `contract`: the public output lacks fields its readers need.\n240: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every reader of the old doctor block is updated: `rg -n \"DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS|doctorCommandString\" $ADV --glob '!dist'`.\n241: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Every reader of `ownerSkillId` and `command` is listed: `rg -n \"ownerSkillId|\\.command\\b\" $ADV $HK .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts --glob '!dist' --glob '!node_modules'`.\n242: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The renderer matrix axes from `plan.md` are each a test row.\n243: - [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on.\n244: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n245: \n246: ---\n247: \n248: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n249: ## Security\n250: \n251: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] Every label part passes `sanitizeSkillLabel`.\n252: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] The relabel script prints no prompt text (T035).\n253: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n254: \n255: ---\n256: \n257: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n258: ## Documentation\n259: \n260: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same fields and numbers.\n261: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The hook doc, the feature catalog entry and the bridges README match the code (T038 to T040).\n262: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n263: \n264: ---\n265: \n266: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n267: ## File Organization\n268: \n269: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Probes, timing runs, the relabel script and capture output live in `scratch/` only.\n270: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n271: \n272: ---\n273: \n274: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n275: ## Verification Summary\n276: \n277: | Category | Total | Verified |\n278: |----------|-------|----------|\n279: | P0 Items | 12 | 1/12 |\n280: | P1 Items | 11 | 1/11 |\n281: | P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n282: \n283: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-12\n284: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794529051510,"end":1794529051563}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794529053387,"sessionID":"ses_e2dbc3ae5ffes1Ef3Xp19Y6IEG","part":{"id":"prt_1d2444acb001bPLWlmu7Le1Js7","sessionID":"ses_e2dbc3ae5ffes1Ef3Xp19Y6IEG","messageID":"msg_1d244378a0010Vj0dtfR2HCHr1","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"c56fd0494e75249c1a6f53fa6c65986311cd0f4c","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":676,"output":109,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":16768,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794529055330,"sessionID":"ses_e2dbc3ae5ffes1Ef3Xp19Y6IEG","part":{"id":"prt_1d2445262001UiWHSrNLzuAs8T","sessionID":"ses_e2dbc3ae5ffes1Ef3Xp19Y6IEG","messageID":"msg_1d2444ad4001lFhjPrk6p7NTTj","type":"step-start","snapshot":"f8c991ad8ea1503bb4df78c7a68fab0d635c64b2"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794529063152,"sessionID":"ses_e2dbc3ae5ffes1Ef3Xp19Y6IEG","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2446c35001R113k6wcGNNqN1","sessionID":"ses_e2dbc3ae5ffes1Ef3Xp19Y6IEG","messageID":"msg_1d2444ad4001lFhjPrk6p7NTTj","type":"tool","id":"call_5b7587bc945644559dfe746d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md, lines 1-205\n1: ---\n2: title: Skill Advisor Hook Reference\n3: description: Operator contract for the maintained Skill Advisor adapters across Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, and the OpenCode plugin. Surfaces a prompt-safe routing brief on each user prompt; advisory only and fail-open.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"skill advisor hook reference\"\n6:   - \"native-first advisor hooks\"\n7:   - \"advisor hook runtime matrix\"\n8:   - \"opencode plugin bridge\"\n9:   - \"advisor hook smoke tests\"\n10: importance_tier: important\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 3.6.5.0\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Skill Advisor Hook Reference\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n20: \n21: The Skill Advisor concern surfaces prompt-safe routing context at the moment a user submits a prompt: it scores the prompt against the maintained skill graph and, when a match clears the confidence threshold, injects a brief recommending the matching skill(s). The brief is advisory: it never replaces explicit skill loading, never persists raw prompt text, and never blocks the prompt on an advisor failure.\n22: \n23: The maintained advisor implementation lives in `system-skill-advisor/runtime/`. The four editor runtimes (Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin) each carry a thin `user-prompt-submit` shim in `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/<runtime>/` that resolves and spawns the compiled advisor in `system-skill-advisor`. The real brief-building, scoring, freshness, and rendering logic lives in the advisor package. Pi carries a native TypeScript extension that imports the same advisor module in-process (Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old two-process blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send). OpenCode integrates through the committed plugin at `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, which shells out to the advisor CLI.\n24: \n25: The single most important property is that it **fails open**: the prompt always proceeds. When the advisor call times out, fails or finds no route, the handler and the OpenCode plugin emit the directives fallback instead of a brief. An unparseable payload, an unhandled error or a shim that cannot relay its child resolves to `{}`. Every adapter honors the `skill-advisor` kill-switch, default-on.\n26: \n27: Paths beginning with `runtime/` in the package-local tables resolve from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/` (for the shims) or `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/` (for the advisor). Paths beginning with `.skilled/` are repository-root relative.\n28: \n29: ---\n30: \n31: ## 2. WHAT IT DOES\n32: \n33: On each user-prompt event the adapter:\n34: \n35: 1. **Kill-switch.** Checks `isHookEnabled('skill-advisor')` (master `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` or the `skill-advisor` family). Disabled → empty/skipped prompt-safe output.\n36: 2. **Read the prompt + workspace.** Resolves the workspace root (install-anchored walk, not CWD-relative, so the hook stays correct off-root), reads the prompt text (bounded), and resolves the session id.\n37: 3. **Prompt gate.** `skippedAdvisorResultFor` uses `shouldFireAdvisor` to decline skip commands, short acknowledgements and prompts below its length threshold. A declined prompt returns a skipped result and does not spawn the CLI.\n38: 4. **CLI front door.** The hook calls `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli`, which runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` within the `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` budget (2,500 ms by default). It writes the request to the CLI's stdin, so the prompt never appears in the process table. The request carries at most the prompt's first 10,000 characters, the most `advisor_recommend` accepts, so a longer prompt is routed on its head instead of failing open. The Claude shim sets the child budget to 2,200 ms when the operator has not set the variable. An operator value above about 2,200 ms lets the shim kill the hook at 2,500 ms first, so the turn gets `{}`. The CLI owns the warm-daemon probe, starts the daemon when the socket is cold and falls back to the local Python scorer with a `degraded` result. The request carries `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. It also carries `compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, because each route lookup is a subprocess inside the hook's budget and the brief leads with the top pick. The hook keeps the `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. A daemon still running an older build rejects these options with JSON-RPC `-32602`, and the CLI retries once without them.\n39: 5. **Render.** `renderAdvisorBrief` produces the model-visible `Advisor:` text. When there is no brief, the handler emits `renderAdvisorFallbackDirective`: one status line, then the directives block. The line reads `Advisor: outage (<status>)` with the command to route by hand when the advisor failed or timed out, `Advisor: no skill matched.` when it answered with nothing above threshold, and `Advisor: prompt skipped.` when the prompt gate declined. The `/doctor:setup` hint appears on no-match and outage lines for prompts that use set up, set-up or setup wording, install or reinstall wording including installation and installer, configure or configuration wording or `check` followed within three words by environment, env, config, hooks, tools, tooling, toolchain or skilled. The no-match line ends with ` For setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup.` The outage line places `for setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup;` before the hand-route command so it stays last. Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution.\n40: 6. **Directive-lifecycle dedup.** `decideDirectiveLifecycleDelivery` suppresses a re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence, so a repeated prompt does not re-inject an identical brief. A repeat in a known session keeps the first line, a route or a fallback status, and drops the directives block.\n41: 7. **Emit.** Native adapters emit a `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` JSON envelope. OpenCode appends to `output.system` via `experimental.chat.system.transform`. Pi sends a model-visible message.\n42: \n43: The injected brief begins with `Advisor:` and names the recommended skill(s) with their confidence. A doctor command appears as its runnable `/doctor:` string on the top line or under a skill as an `Also:` second line. The handler returns `{}` when the hook is disabled, input cannot be parsed or an unhandled exception occurs. A shim also returns `{}` when it cannot resolve or relay valid child output, including on timeout. When the handler has no brief, it emits the directives fallback.\n44: \n45: ---\n46: \n47: ## 3. PER-RUNTIME DELIVERY\n48: \n49: Every native runtime and Pi run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`. The OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. The native adapters differ in prompt event, transport and delivery channel.\n50: \n51: | Runtime | Adapter | Event / wiring | Payload difference it handles | Delivery |\n52: |---|---|---|---|---|\n53: | **Claude** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `system-skill-advisor/.../dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.claude/settings.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 3s | Shim resolves the advisor target by walking up to the `.opencode` ancestor (install-anchored, not CWD-relative). Bounded stdin (1 MiB), bounded child stdio, 2.5s child timeout, `SIGKILL` on timeout | `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` JSON on stdout. `{}` on any failure |\n54: | **Codex** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.codex/hooks.json`, timeout 3s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope on resolution failure | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n55: | **Cursor** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js` | `beforeSubmitPrompt` in `.cursor/hooks.json`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n56: | **Devin** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n57: | **Pi** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` (real file, re-exported by its one-line `.pi/extensions/` entry) | `user_input` / prompt event via `.pi/extensions/` | Imports the advisor module **in-process** (not a subprocess). Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send. In-process calls remove the stall and let the module-level prompt cache work. Captures raw user text (bounded 32 KiB, 64-session LRU). The in-process call passes `runtime: 'pi'` and races a timer of the advisor budget plus 300 ms, delivering the fallback directives if the call hangs | Model-visible message. Delivery-state machine suppresses same-session re-delivery |\n58: | **OpenCode** | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | Plugin, loaded by OpenCode's flat glob over `.opencode/plugins/`. `experimental.chat.system.transform` per prompt, `event` for session lifecycle, `tool` for status | Shells out to the advisor CLI (bounded timeout, stdout cap 256 KiB, grace termination), TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup, transform-dedup integration | Brief appended to `output.system`. `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` tool returns a key=value report (no raw path leakage) |\n59: \n60: OpenCode has no source-hook adapter in `system-spec-kit`. Its prompt-time integration is the committed plugin, which shells out to the advisor CLI and inherits the shared render contract. The hooks-tree index at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/` mirrors the per-runtime shims and the OpenCode plugin via relative symlinks. This README is the symlink target.\n61: \n62: ---\n63: \n64: ## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n65: \n66: ```text\n67: system-skill-advisor/hooks/\n68: +-- skill-advisor-hook.md            # this reference (symlinked from .skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/README.md)\n69: +-- skill-advisor-hook-validation.md # validation/audit detail\n70: +-- claude/\n71: |   +-- README.md\n72: |   +-- directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts\n73: |   `-- user-prompt-submit.ts         # real advisor handler (Claude shape)\n74: +-- pi/\n75: |   +-- README.md\n76: |   `-- prompt-advisor.ts             # real Pi extension (.pi/extensions/ re-exports it)\n77: `-- lib/\n78:     +-- README.md\n79:     +-- directive-lifecycle.ts, directive-lifecycle-contract.ts, directive-lifecycle-file-store.ts\n80:     +-- directive-lifecycle-store.py, directive-lifecycle-vectors.json\n81:     `-- skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts\n82: \n83: system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.{ts,js}  # thin shims (claude/codex/cursor/devin)\n84: system-skill-advisor/runtime/\n85: +-- dist/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.js   # compiled advisor the shims spawn\n86: +-- lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts, render.ts, metrics.ts, subprocess.ts\n87: `-- scripts/skill_advisor.py                      # standalone Python advisor CLI\n88: .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js         # OpenCode plugin\n89: ```\n90: \n91: ---\n92: \n93: ## 5. KEY FILES\n94: \n95: | File | Responsibility |\n96: |---|---|\n97: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` | The real advisor handler (Claude shape). Builds the brief, runs the CLI fallback, renders, applies directive-lifecycle dedup, emits the `additionalContext` envelope, persists a diagnostic record. The codex/cursor/devin siblings share the same advisor core over their runtime's payload shape. |\n98: | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.ts` | Thin process-boundary shims. Resolve the advisor target by walking up to the `.opencode` ancestor, spawn the compiled advisor with bounded stdin/stdio/timeout, and relay its stdout (or `{}` on any failure). |\n99: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` | Native Pi extension. Imports the advisor module in-process, captures raw user text (bounded LRU), runs a delivery-state machine that suppresses same-session re-delivery, and sends the brief as a model-visible message. Races the advisor call against a deadline of the advisor budget plus 300 ms and delivers the fallback directives if it hangs. |\n100: | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | OpenCode plugin. `experimental.chat.system.transform` spawns the bridge and appends the brief to `output.system`. `event` manages session lifecycle and cache invalidation. `tool: spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` returns a sanitized status report. TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup and transform-dedup integration. |\n101: | `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs` | The CLI front door the OpenCode plugin spawns. Receives the `advisor_recommend` command line, returns the JSON payload on stdout. |\n102: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts` | The brief builder: scoring, freshness, status, confidence/uncertainty. |\n103: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts` | `renderAdvisorBrief` / `renderAdvisorFallbackDirective`, produces the model-visible text. |\n104: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/directive-lifecycle.ts` | Directive-lifecycle dedup: decides whether a directive should be re-delivered to a session within its cadence. |\n105: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli` is the hook's CLI caller. It runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` with the hook timeout and sends the request on stdin. The CLI owns daemon startup and local-scorer fallback. The function resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root. It searches `.skilled` first and `.opencode` second. |\n106: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py` | Standalone Python advisor CLI. The advisor CLI runs it as the local scorer when the daemon is unreachable. The hook never calls it directly. |\n107: \n108: ---\n109: \n110: ## 6. CONFIGURATION\n111: \n112: The advisor is enabled by default. Truthy disable values are `1`, `true`, `yes`, and `on` (case-insensitive) for the shared resolver.\n113: \n114: | Variable | Effect |\n115: |---|---|\n116: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1` | Canonical kill-switch. Every adapter checks `isHookEnabled('skill-advisor')` and returns empty/skipped prompt-safe output. |\n117: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Alias. Disables the native adapters. |\n118: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Alias. Disables the OpenCode plugin. |\n119: | `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias for the native adapters. The standalone Python CLI (`skill_advisor.py`) reads only this name, set to exactly `1`, from `runtime/schemas/compat-contract.json`. |\n120: | `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias for the OpenCode plugin. |\n121: | `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` | Master switch that disables this concern along with every other repo hook. |\n122: \n123: Additional controls: `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL=1` (force local Python fallback where supported) and `--force-native` / `--force-local` / `--threshold` / `--stdin` (Python shim flags, default threshold `0.8`). `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` (default 3000) is owned by the `system-skill-advisor` hub: its live consumers are `runtime/lib/subprocess.ts`, `skill-advisor-brief.ts`, the OpenCode bridge and `skill_advisor.py`. On timeout the OpenCode bridge serves prompt-safe stale context with a timeout marker. OpenCode tuning: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CACHE_TTL_MS` (default 5 min), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_TOKENS` (default 80), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_BRIEF_CHARS` (default 2 KiB), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_PROMPT_BYTES` (default 64 KiB, measured on the whole stdin request after JSON escaping), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_COMPILED_ROUTE_BOUNDING` (compiled-route summary bounding).\n124: \n125: Set a flag inline for one command, export it for a session, or persist it in `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env` (copied from `hook-flags.env.example`, gitignored). The environment always wins over the file, so a persisted default can be overridden for a single session.\n126: \n127: ---\n128: \n129: ## 7. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n130: \n131: | Boundary | Rule |\n132: |---|---|\n133: | Advisory only | Hooks surface prompt-safe routing context. They do not replace explicit skill loading, persist raw prompt text, or block the user prompt on advisor failures. |\n134: | Fail-open | All adapters let the prompt proceed. A failed or empty advisor call yields the directives fallback. A parsing failure or unhandled error yields `{}`. The shims return `{}` on `TARGET_UNRESOLVED`, `CHILD_TIMEOUT`, `NONZERO_EXIT`, `EMPTY_OUTPUT`, `INVALID_JSON`, `INPUT_OVERFLOW`, and `SPAWN_ERROR`. |\n135: | Freshness | Freshness states `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`. Status values `ok`, `skipped`, `degraded`, `fail_open`. Default confidence/uncertainty `0.8 / 0.35` unless overridden. |\n136: | Privacy | Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution. The OpenCode status tool sanitizes paths (`[configured-node]`, `[skill-advisor-bridge]`). |\n137: | Dedup | Directive-lifecycle dedup suppresses re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence. OpenCode adds transform-dedup across co-resident transforms. The plugin decides same-message transform dedup on the full advisor block before lifecycle reduction, so a repeated transform for the same message is suppressed. |\n138: | Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Records are written only with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` set, and the subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n139: | Bounded | Shims bound stdin (1 MiB), child stdio (1 MiB), child timeout (2.5s), and `SIGKILL` on timeout. OpenCode bounds bridge stdout (256 KiB) and uses grace termination. Pi bounds captured user text (32 KiB, 64-session LRU). |\n140: | Output | Native adapters emit one `additionalContext` JSON on stdout. OpenCode appends to `output.system`. Pi sends a model-visible message. No adapter writes to the TUI prompt line. |\n141: | Imports | Shims import Node builtins only and spawn the advisor by absolute path. The advisor core imports its `runtime/lib/*` siblings and the shared `hook-flags` resolver. Nothing outside the repo. |\n142: \n143: ### Operator freshness states\n144: \n145: | State | Meaning | Operator Action |\n146: | --- | --- | --- |\n147: | `live` | Current graph generation is trusted. | No action. |\n148: | `stale` | Sources are newer than graph state. | Use scored recommendations with a caveat, then rebuild. |\n149: | `absent` | Required graph state is missing. | Rebuild. Empty recommendations are expected until repaired. |\n150: | `unavailable` | Status cannot be read. | Inspect daemon logs and use a supported fallback. |\n151: \n152: ---\n153: \n154: ## 8. VALIDATION\n155: \n156: Build both maintained packages:\n157: \n158: ```bash\n159: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run build\n160: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n161: ```\n162: \n163: Expected result: both builds succeed and `dist/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.js` are produced.\n164: \n165: ```bash\n166: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run typecheck\n167: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime test -- --reporter=default\n168: node --test .opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs\n169: ```\n170: \n171: Expected result: no type errors. All advisor package tests pass. The OpenCode plugin test passes.\n172: \n173: Native smoke tests (each targets an existing compiled file):\n174: \n175: ```bash\n176: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"update documentation with DQI checks\",\"cwd\":\"'\"$PWD\"'\"}' | \\\n177:   node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js\n178: ```\n179: \n180: Expected: `{}` or `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` beginning with `Advisor:`. Repeat for the `codex`, `cursor`, and `devin` siblings.\n181: \n182: OpenCode plugin CLI smoke test:\n183: \n184: ```bash\n185: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"save this conversation context to memory\",\"options\":{\"topK\":3,\"includeAttribution\":false,\"includeAbstainReasons\":true,\"confidenceThreshold\":0.8,\"uncertaintyThreshold\":0.35}}' \\\n186:   | node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --format json\n187: ```\n188: \n189: Installation drift check (from a linked worktree with the required worktree flag):\n190: \n191: ```bash\n192: node .skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs --check --allow-worktree\n193: ```\n194: \n195: This compares the repository's maintained Codex registration and adapter paths. A report about the user-global installation is workstation state, not a repository defect.\n196: \n197: ---\n198: \n199: ## 9. RELATED\n200: \n201: - [`skill-advisor-hook-validation.md`](skill-advisor-hook-validation.md): validation and audit detail for this concern.\n202: - [`claude/README.md`](claude/README.md), [`pi/README.md`](pi/README.md), [`lib/README.md`](lib/README.md): per-surface detail.\n203: - [`../../system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/README.md`](../../system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/README.md): the owning skill's hook contract (where the shims live).\n204: - [`../../../hooks/README.md`](../../../hooks/README.md): the unified hooks tree with the kill-switch index and coverage matrix.\n205: - [`../../../../.opencode/plugins/README.md`](../../../../.opencode/plugins/README.md): the OpenCode plugins folder that loads `system-skill-advisor.js`.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md, lines 1-205\n1: ---\n2: title: Skill Advisor Hook Reference\n3: description: Operator contract for the maintained Skill Advisor adapters across Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, and the OpenCode plugin. Surfaces a prompt-safe routing brief on each user prompt; advisory only and fail-open.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"skill advisor hook reference\"\n6:   - \"native-first advisor hooks\"\n7:   - \"advisor hook runtime matrix\"\n8:   - \"opencode plugin bridge\"\n9:   - \"advisor hook smoke tests\"\n10: importance_tier: important\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 3.6.5.0\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Skill Advisor Hook Reference\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n20: \n21: The Skill Advisor concern surfaces prompt-safe routing context at the moment a user submits a prompt: it scores the prompt against the maintained skill graph and, when a match clears the confidence threshold, injects a brief recommending the matching skill(s). The brief is advisory: it never replaces explicit skill loading, never persists raw prompt text, and never blocks the prompt on an advisor failure.\n22: \n23: The maintained advisor implementation lives in `system-skill-advisor/runtime/`. The four editor runtimes (Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin) each carry a thin `user-prompt-submit` shim in `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/<runtime>/` that resolves and spawns the compiled advisor in `system-skill-advisor`. The real brief-building, scoring, freshness, and rendering logic lives in the advisor package. Pi carries a native TypeScript extension that imports the same advisor module in-process (Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old two-process blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send). OpenCode integrates through the committed plugin at `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, which shells out to the advisor CLI.\n24: \n25: The single most important property is that it **fails open**: the prompt always proceeds. When the advisor call times out, fails or finds no route, the handler and the OpenCode plugin emit the directives fallback instead of a brief. An unparseable payload, an unhandled error or a shim that cannot relay its child resolves to `{}`. Every adapter honors the `skill-advisor` kill-switch, default-on.\n26: \n27: Paths beginning with `runtime/` in the package-local tables resolve from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/` (for the shims) or `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/` (for the advisor). Paths beginning with `.skilled/` are repository-root relative.\n28: \n29: ---\n30: \n31: ## 2. WHAT IT DOES\n32: \n33: On each user-prompt event the adapter:\n34: \n35: 1. **Kill-switch.** Checks `isHookEnabled('skill-advisor')` (master `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` or the `skill-advisor` family). Disabled → empty/skipped prompt-safe output.\n36: 2. **Read the prompt + workspace.** Resolves the workspace root (install-anchored walk, not CWD-relative, so the hook stays correct off-root), reads the prompt text (bounded), and resolves the session id.\n37: 3. **Prompt gate.** `skippedAdvisorResultFor` uses `shouldFireAdvisor` to decline skip commands, short acknowledgements and prompts below its length threshold. A declined prompt returns a skipped result and does not spawn the CLI.\n38: 4. **CLI front door.** The hook calls `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli`, which runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` within the `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` budget (2,500 ms by default). It writes the request to the CLI's stdin, so the prompt never appears in the process table. The request carries at most the prompt's first 10,000 characters, the most `advisor_recommend` accepts, so a longer prompt is routed on its head instead of failing open. The Claude shim sets the child budget to 2,200 ms when the operator has not set the variable. An operator value above about 2,200 ms lets the shim kill the hook at 2,500 ms first, so the turn gets `{}`. The CLI owns the warm-daemon probe, starts the daemon when the socket is cold and falls back to the local Python scorer with a `degraded` result. The request carries `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. It also carries `compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, because each route lookup is a subprocess inside the hook's budget and the brief leads with the top pick. The hook keeps the `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. A daemon still running an older build rejects these options with JSON-RPC `-32602`, and the CLI retries once without them.\n39: 5. **Render.** `renderAdvisorBrief` produces the model-visible `Advisor:` text. When there is no brief, the handler emits `renderAdvisorFallbackDirective`: one status line, then the directives block. The line reads `Advisor: outage (<status>)` with the command to route by hand when the advisor failed or timed out, `Advisor: no skill matched.` when it answered with nothing above threshold, and `Advisor: prompt skipped.` when the prompt gate declined. The `/doctor:setup` hint appears on no-match and outage lines for prompts that use set up, set-up or setup wording, install or reinstall wording including installation and installer, configure or configuration wording or `check` followed within three words by environment, env, config, hooks, tools, tooling, toolchain or skilled. The no-match line ends with ` For setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup.` The outage line places `for setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup;` before the hand-route command so it stays last. Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution.\n40: 6. **Directive-lifecycle dedup.** `decideDirectiveLifecycleDelivery` suppresses a re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence, so a repeated prompt does not re-inject an identical brief. A repeat in a known session keeps the first line, a route or a fallback status, and drops the directives block.\n41: 7. **Emit.** Native adapters emit a `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` JSON envelope. OpenCode appends to `output.system` via `experimental.chat.system.transform`. Pi sends a model-visible message.\n42: \n43: The injected brief begins with `Advisor:` and names the recommended skill(s) with their confidence. A doctor command appears as its runnable `/doctor:` string on the top line or under a skill as an `Also:` second line. The handler returns `{}` when the hook is disabled, input cannot be parsed or an unhandled exception occurs. A shim also returns `{}` when it cannot resolve or relay valid child output, including on timeout. When the handler has no brief, it emits the directives fallback.\n44: \n45: ---\n46: \n47: ## 3. PER-RUNTIME DELIVERY\n48: \n49: Every native runtime and Pi run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`. The OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. The native adapters differ in prompt event, transport and delivery channel.\n50: \n51: | Runtime | Adapter | Event / wiring | Payload difference it handles | Delivery |\n52: |---|---|---|---|---|\n53: | **Claude** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `system-skill-advisor/.../dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.claude/settings.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 3s | Shim resolves the advisor target by walking up to the `.opencode` ancestor (install-anchored, not CWD-relative). Bounded stdin (1 MiB), bounded child stdio, 2.5s child timeout, `SIGKILL` on timeout | `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` JSON on stdout. `{}` on any failure |\n54: | **Codex** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.codex/hooks.json`, timeout 3s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope on resolution failure | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n55: | **Cursor** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js` | `beforeSubmitPrompt` in `.cursor/hooks.json`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n56: | **Devin** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n57: | **Pi** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` (real file, re-exported by its one-line `.pi/extensions/` entry) | `user_input` / prompt event via `.pi/extensions/` | Imports the advisor module **in-process** (not a subprocess). Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send. In-process calls remove the stall and let the module-level prompt cache work. Captures raw user text (bounded 32 KiB, 64-session LRU). The in-process call passes `runtime: 'pi'` and races a timer of the advisor budget plus 300 ms, delivering the fallback directives if the call hangs | Model-visible message. Delivery-state machine suppresses same-session re-delivery |\n58: | **OpenCode** | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | Plugin, loaded by OpenCode's flat glob over `.opencode/plugins/`. `experimental.chat.system.transform` per prompt, `event` for session lifecycle, `tool` for status | Shells out to the advisor CLI (bounded timeout, stdout cap 256 KiB, grace termination), TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup, transform-dedup integration | Brief appended to `output.system`. `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` tool returns a key=value report (no raw path leakage) |\n59: \n60: OpenCode has no source-hook adapter in `system-spec-kit`. Its prompt-time integration is the committed plugin, which shells out to the advisor CLI and inherits the shared render contract. The hooks-tree index at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/` mirrors the per-runtime shims and the OpenCode plugin via relative symlinks. This README is the symlink target.\n61: \n62: ---\n63: \n64: ## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n65: \n66: ```text\n67: system-skill-advisor/hooks/\n68: +-- skill-advisor-hook.md            # this reference (symlinked from .skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/README.md)\n69: +-- skill-advisor-hook-validation.md # validation/audit detail\n70: +-- claude/\n71: |   +-- README.md\n72: |   +-- directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts\n73: |   `-- user-prompt-submit.ts         # real advisor handler (Claude shape)\n74: +-- pi/\n75: |   +-- README.md\n76: |   `-- prompt-advisor.ts             # real Pi extension (.pi/extensions/ re-exports it)\n77: `-- lib/\n78:     +-- README.md\n79:     +-- directive-lifecycle.ts, directive-lifecycle-contract.ts, directive-lifecycle-file-store.ts\n80:     +-- directive-lifecycle-store.py, directive-lifecycle-vectors.json\n81:     `-- skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts\n82: \n83: system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.{ts,js}  # thin shims (claude/codex/cursor/devin)\n84: system-skill-advisor/runtime/\n85: +-- dist/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.js   # compiled advisor the shims spawn\n86: +-- lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts, render.ts, metrics.ts, subprocess.ts\n87: `-- scripts/skill_advisor.py                      # standalone Python advisor CLI\n88: .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js         # OpenCode plugin\n89: ```\n90: \n91: ---\n92: \n93: ## 5. KEY FILES\n94: \n95: | File | Responsibility |\n96: |---|---|\n97: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` | The real advisor handler (Claude shape). Builds the brief, runs the CLI fallback, renders, applies directive-lifecycle dedup, emits the `additionalContext` envelope, persists a diagnostic record. The codex/cursor/devin siblings share the same advisor core over their runtime's payload shape. |\n98: | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.ts` | Thin process-boundary shims. Resolve the advisor target by walking up to the `.opencode` ancestor, spawn the compiled advisor with bounded stdin/stdio/timeout, and relay its stdout (or `{}` on any failure). |\n99: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` | Native Pi extension. Imports the advisor module in-process, captures raw user text (bounded LRU), runs a delivery-state machine that suppresses same-session re-delivery, and sends the brief as a model-visible message. Races the advisor call against a deadline of the advisor budget plus 300 ms and delivers the fallback directives if it hangs. |\n100: | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | OpenCode plugin. `experimental.chat.system.transform` spawns the bridge and appends the brief to `output.system`. `event` manages session lifecycle and cache invalidation. `tool: spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` returns a sanitized status report. TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup and transform-dedup integration. |\n101: | `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs` | The CLI front door the OpenCode plugin spawns. Receives the `advisor_recommend` command line, returns the JSON payload on stdout. |\n102: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts` | The brief builder: scoring, freshness, status, confidence/uncertainty. |\n103: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts` | `renderAdvisorBrief` / `renderAdvisorFallbackDirective`, produces the model-visible text. |\n104: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/directive-lifecycle.ts` | Directive-lifecycle dedup: decides whether a directive should be re-delivered to a session within its cadence. |\n105: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli` is the hook's CLI caller. It runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` with the hook timeout and sends the request on stdin. The CLI owns daemon startup and local-scorer fallback. The function resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root. It searches `.skilled` first and `.opencode` second. |\n106: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py` | Standalone Python advisor CLI. The advisor CLI runs it as the local scorer when the daemon is unreachable. The hook never calls it directly. |\n107: \n108: ---\n109: \n110: ## 6. CONFIGURATION\n111: \n112: The advisor is enabled by default. Truthy disable values are `1`, `true`, `yes`, and `on` (case-insensitive) for the shared resolver.\n113: \n114: | Variable | Effect |\n115: |---|---|\n116: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1` | Canonical kill-switch. Every adapter checks `isHookEnabled('skill-advisor')` and returns empty/skipped prompt-safe output. |\n117: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Alias. Disables the native adapters. |\n118: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Alias. Disables the OpenCode plugin. |\n119: | `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias for the native adapters. The standalone Python CLI (`skill_advisor.py`) reads only this name, set to exactly `1`, from `runtime/schemas/compat-contract.json`. |\n120: | `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias for the OpenCode plugin. |\n121: | `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` | Master switch that disables this concern along with every other repo hook. |\n122: \n123: Additional controls: `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL=1` (force local Python fallback where supported) and `--force-native` / `--force-local` / `--threshold` / `--stdin` (Python shim flags, default threshold `0.8`). `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` (default 3000) is owned by the `system-skill-advisor` hub: its live consumers are `runtime/lib/subprocess.ts`, `skill-advisor-brief.ts`, the OpenCode bridge and `skill_advisor.py`. On timeout the OpenCode bridge serves prompt-safe stale context with a timeout marker. OpenCode tuning: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CACHE_TTL_MS` (default 5 min), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_TOKENS` (default 80), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_BRIEF_CHARS` (default 2 KiB), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_PROMPT_BYTES` (default 64 KiB, measured on the whole stdin request after JSON escaping), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_COMPILED_ROUTE_BOUNDING` (compiled-route summary bounding).\n124: \n125: Set a flag inline for one command, export it for a session, or persist it in `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env` (copied from `hook-flags.env.example`, gitignored). The environment always wins over the file, so a persisted default can be overridden for a single session.\n126: \n127: ---\n128: \n129: ## 7. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n130: \n131: | Boundary | Rule |\n132: |---|---|\n133: | Advisory only | Hooks surface prompt-safe routing context. They do not replace explicit skill loading, persist raw prompt text, or block the user prompt on advisor failures. |\n134: | Fail-open | All adapters let the prompt proceed. A failed or empty advisor call yields the directives fallback. A parsing failure or unhandled error yields `{}`. The shims return `{}` on `TARGET_UNRESOLVED`, `CHILD_TIMEOUT`, `NONZERO_EXIT`, `EMPTY_OUTPUT`, `INVALID_JSON`, `INPUT_OVERFLOW`, and `SPAWN_ERROR`. |\n135: | Freshness | Freshness states `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`. Status values `ok`, `skipped`, `degraded`, `fail_open`. Default confidence/uncertainty `0.8 / 0.35` unless overridden. |\n136: | Privacy | Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution. The OpenCode status tool sanitizes paths (`[configured-node]`, `[skill-advisor-bridge]`). |\n137: | Dedup | Directive-lifecycle dedup suppresses re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence. OpenCode adds transform-dedup across co-resident transforms. The plugin decides same-message transform dedup on the full advisor block before lifecycle reduction, so a repeated transform for the same message is suppressed. |\n138: | Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Records are written only with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` set, and the subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n139: | Bounded | Shims bound stdin (1 MiB), child stdio (1 MiB), child timeout (2.5s), and `SIGKILL` on timeout. OpenCode bounds bridge stdout (256 KiB) and uses grace termination. Pi bounds captured user text (32 KiB, 64-session LRU). |\n140: | Output | Native adapters emit one `additionalContext` JSON on stdout. OpenCode appends to `output.system`. Pi sends a model-visible message. No adapter writes to the TUI prompt line. |\n141: | Imports | Shims import Node builtins only and spawn the advisor by absolute path. The advisor core imports its `runtime/lib/*` siblings and the shared `hook-flags` resolver. Nothing outside the repo. |\n142: \n143: ### Operator freshness states\n144: \n145: | State | Meaning | Operator Action |\n146: | --- | --- | --- |\n147: | `live` | Current graph generation is trusted. | No action. |\n148: | `stale` | Sources are newer than graph state. | Use scored recommendations with a caveat, then rebuild. |\n149: | `absent` | Required graph state is missing. | Rebuild. Empty recommendations are expected until repaired. |\n150: | `unavailable` | Status cannot be read. | Inspect daemon logs and use a supported fallback. |\n151: \n152: ---\n153: \n154: ## 8. VALIDATION\n155: \n156: Build both maintained packages:\n157: \n158: ```bash\n159: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run build\n160: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n161: ```\n162: \n163: Expected result: both builds succeed and `dist/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.js` are produced.\n164: \n165: ```bash\n166: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run typecheck\n167: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime test -- --reporter=default\n168: node --test .opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs\n169: ```\n170: \n171: Expected result: no type errors. All advisor package tests pass. The OpenCode plugin test passes.\n172: \n173: Native smoke tests (each targets an existing compiled file):\n174: \n175: ```bash\n176: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"update documentation with DQI checks\",\"cwd\":\"'\"$PWD\"'\"}' | \\\n177:   node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js\n178: ```\n179: \n180: Expected: `{}` or `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` beginning with `Advisor:`. Repeat for the `codex`, `cursor`, and `devin` siblings.\n181: \n182: OpenCode plugin CLI smoke test:\n183: \n184: ```bash\n185: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"save this conversation context to memory\",\"options\":{\"topK\":3,\"includeAttribution\":false,\"includeAbstainReasons\":true,\"confidenceThreshold\":0.8,\"uncertaintyThreshold\":0.35}}' \\\n186:   | node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --format json\n187: ```\n188: \n189: Installation drift check (from a linked worktree with the required worktree flag):\n190: \n191: ```bash\n192: node .skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs --check --allow-worktree\n193: ```\n194: \n195: This compares the repository's maintained Codex registration and adapter paths. A report about the user-global installation is workstation state, not a repository defect.\n196: \n197: ---\n198: \n199: ## 9. RELATED\n200: \n201: - [`skill-advisor-hook-validation.md`](skill-advisor-hook-validation.md): validation and audit detail for this concern.\n202: - [`claude/README.md`](claude/README.md), [`pi/README.md`](pi/README.md), [`lib/README.md`](lib/README.md): per-surface detail.\n203: - [`../../system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/README.md`](../../system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/README.md): the owning skill's hook contract (where the shims live).\n204: - [`../../../hooks/README.md`](../../../hooks/README.md): the unified hooks tree with the kill-switch index and coverage matrix.\n205: - [`../../../../.opencode/plugins/README.md`](../../../../.opencode/plugins/README.md): the OpenCode plugins folder that loads `system-skill-advisor.js`."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794529061941,"end":1794529063152}}}}
