{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794529114938,"sessionID":"ses_e2dbc3ae5ffes1Ef3Xp19Y6IEG","part":{"partID":"prt_1d24538ff0015z4KkOzb83bHcF","sessionID":"ses_e2dbc3ae5ffes1Ef3Xp19Y6IEG","messageID":"msg_1d24528c1001LZLWtez5CLZZbe","type":"tool","id":"call_c3144125c753451cbceb870b","tool":"grep","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"degraded|→ /speckit:save","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md"},"output":"Found 2 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:\n  Line 38: 4. **CLI front door.** The hook calls `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli`, which runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` within the `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` budget (2,500 ms by default). It writes the request to the CLI's stdin, so the prompt never appears in the process table. The request carries at most the prompt's first 10,000 characters, the most `advisor_recommend` accepts, so a longer prompt is routed on its head instead of failing open. The Claude shim sets the child budget to 2,200 ms when the operator has not set the variable. An operator value above about 2,200 ms lets the shim kill the hook at 2,500 ms first, so the turn gets `{}`. The CLI owns the warm-daemon probe, starts the daemon when the socket is cold and falls back to the local Python scorer with a `degraded` result. The request carries `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. It also carries `compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, because each route lookup is a subprocess inside the hook's budget and the brief leads with the top pick. The hook keeps the `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. A daemon still running an older build rejects these options with JSON-RPC `-32602`, and the CLI retries once without them.\n\n  Line 135: | Freshness | Freshness states `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`. Status values `ok`, `skipped`, `degraded`, `fail_open`. Default confidence/uncertainty `0.8 / 0.35` unless overridden. |\n","title":"grep","metadata":{"metadata":{"matches":2,"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 2 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:\n  Line 38: 4. **CLI front door.** The hook calls `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli`, which runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` within the `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` budget (2,500 ms by default). It writes the request to the CLI's stdin, so the prompt never appears in the process table. The request carries at most the prompt's first 10,000 characters, the most `advisor_recommend` accepts, so a longer prompt is routed on its head instead of failing open. The Claude shim sets the child budget to 2,200 ms when the operator has not set the variable. An operator value above about 2,200 ms lets the shim kill the hook at 2,500 ms first, so the turn gets `{}`. The CLI owns the warm-daemon probe, starts the daemon when the socket is cold and falls back to the local Python scorer with a `degraded` result. The request carries `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. It also carries `compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, because each route lookup is a subprocess inside the hook's budget and the brief leads with the top pick. The hook keeps the `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. A daemon still running an older build rejects these options with JSON-RPC `-32602`, and the CLI retries once without them.\n\n  Line 135: | Freshness | Freshness states `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`. Status values `ok`, `skipped`, `degraded`, `fail_open`. Default confidence/uncertainty `0.8 / 0.35` unless overridden. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"pattern\":\"degraded|→ /speckit:save\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794529114367,"end":1794529114938}}}}
