{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794529141739,"sessionID":"ses_e2dbc3ae5ffes1Ef3Xp19Y6IEG","part":{"partID":"prt_1d245a0f7001NG8O0l5h10SwTv","sessionID":"ses_e2dbc3ae5ffes1Ef3Xp19Y6IEG","messageID":"msg_1d2459b77001xJxyFBIJ7QR1Uk","type":"tool","id":"call_bfffa78b174a421995698bea","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"→ /speckit:save \\(start\\)|degraded\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"38:4. **CLI front door.** The hook calls `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli`, which runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` within the `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` budget (2,500 ms by default). It writes the request to the CLI's stdin, so the prompt never appears in the process table. The request carries at most the prompt's first 10,000 characters, the most `advisor_recommend` accepts, so a longer prompt is routed on its head instead of failing open. The Claude shim sets the child budget to 2,200 ms when the operator has not set the variable. An operator value above about 2,200 ms lets the shim kill the hook at 2,500 ms first, so the turn gets `{}`. The CLI owns the warm-daemon probe, starts the daemon when the socket is cold and falls back to the local Python scorer with a `degraded` result. The request carries `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. It also carries `compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, because each route lookup is a subprocess inside the hook's budget and the brief leads with the top pick. The hook keeps the `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. A daemon still running an older build rejects these options with JSON-RPC `-32602`, and the CLI retries once without them.\n58:Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n65:When the daemon is unreachable, the CLI runs the local Python scorer and returns `status: ok` with `degraded: true` and `source: local-scorer`. The local scorer returns command row ids, which a reader cannot type, so the CLI rewrites each row before the brief renders:\n67:- A row whose bare slash command appears in the prompt (the row's `command` text before the first space) keeps its command fields: `skillId` is the row id, `kind` is `command`, `command` is the runnable string, `policy` is present when the row has one and `ownerSkillId` names the owning skill. A typed `/speckit:save this session` renders `system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start)`.\n68:- Every other row collapses to its owner skill: `skillId` is `ownerSkillId` and `kind` is `skill`. It is dropped when that skill is already offered, so the degraded brief never repeats a skill.\n70:Rows below the threshold are discarded before either rule applies. The degraded brief therefore keeps the same head form and names a skill that exists rather than a raw row id.\n162:| Freshness | Freshness states `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`. Status values `ok`, `skipped`, `degraded`, `fail_open`. Default confidence/uncertainty `0.8 / 0.35` unless overridden. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"38:4. **CLI front door.** The hook calls `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli`, which runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` within the `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` budget (2,500 ms by default). It writes the request to the CLI's stdin, so the prompt never appears in the process table. The request carries at most the prompt's first 10,000 characters, the most `advisor_recommend` accepts, so a longer prompt is routed on its head instead of failing open. The Claude shim sets the child budget to 2,200 ms when the operator has not set the variable. An operator value above about 2,200 ms lets the shim kill the hook at 2,500 ms first, so the turn gets `{}`. The CLI owns the warm-daemon probe, starts the daemon when the socket is cold and falls back to the local Python scorer with a `degraded` result. The request carries `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. It also carries `compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, because each route lookup is a subprocess inside the hook's budget and the brief leads with the top pick. The hook keeps the `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. A daemon still running an older build rejects these options with JSON-RPC `-32602`, and the CLI retries once without them.\n58:Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n65:When the daemon is unreachable, the CLI runs the local Python scorer and returns `status: ok` with `degraded: true` and `source: local-scorer`. The local scorer returns command row ids, which a reader cannot type, so the CLI rewrites each row before the brief renders:\n67:- A row whose bare slash command appears in the prompt (the row's `command` text before the first space) keeps its command fields: `skillId` is the row id, `kind` is `command`, `command` is the runnable string, `policy` is present when the row has one and `ownerSkillId` names the owning skill. A typed `/speckit:save this session` renders `system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start)`.\n68:- Every other row collapses to its owner skill: `skillId` is `ownerSkillId` and `kind` is `skill`. It is dropped when that skill is already offered, so the degraded brief never repeats a skill.\n70:Rows below the threshold are discarded before either rule applies. The degraded brief therefore keeps the same head form and names a skill that exists rather than a raw row id.\n162:| Freshness | Freshness states `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`. Status values `ok`, `skipped`, `degraded`, `fail_open`. Default confidence/uncertainty `0.8 / 0.35` unless overridden. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"→ /speckit:save \\\\(start\\\\)|degraded\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794529140983,"end":1794529141739}}}}
