{"type":"text","timestamp":1794529162319,"sessionID":"ses_e2dbc3ae5ffes1Ef3Xp19Y6IEG","part":{"id":"prt_1d245e8f3002Pt2ej8PH5QCjwc","sessionID":"ses_e2dbc3ae5ffes1Ef3Xp19Y6IEG","messageID":"msg_1d245e29e001LzlHhhEeUXJEW4","type":"text","text":"T038 complete.\n\n**File written**\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md` — added two subsections under §2: **Brief head form** (`<ownerSkillId or skill> → <command> (<policy>)`, the `use` and `ambiguous` head shapes, `sanitizeSkillLabel` behavior) and **Degraded contract** (local-scorer fallback, `degraded: true`, typed-command rows kept, all other rows collapsed to `ownerSkillId`).\n\n**Verify command output**\n```\n$ rg -n \"→ /speckit:save \\(start\\)|degraded\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\n38:4. **CLI front door.** ... falls back to the local Python scorer with a `degraded` result. ...\n58:Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n65:When the daemon is unreachable, the CLI runs the local Python scorer and returns `status: ok` with `degraded: true` and `source: local-scorer`. ...\n67:- A row whose bare slash command appears in the prompt ... renders `system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start)`.\n68:- Every other row collapses to its owner skill: ...\n70:Rows below the threshold are discarded before either rule applies. The degraded brief therefore keeps the same head form ...\n162:| Freshness | ... Status values `ok`, `skipped`, `degraded`, `fail_open`. ... |\n```\nSix matching lines, exceeding the required two.\n\n**Notes**\n- Did not tick the checkbox in `tasks.md`.\n- No other file touched, no git state changed.","time":{"start":1794529159411,"end":1794529162319}}}
